    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2fafd3bf_abb23151",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/fpmcu/et171/sanok.dts",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-10T12:40:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This CL is not about how the calibration data address should implemented, but in my opinion it is done correctly. The calibration data is an device instance property, not entire driver. I can see a world (not in our application) when you have two finger print sensor connected to your SOC, with different calibration data at different offsets.",
      "parentUuid": "c0118491_ac420343",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "6ce66a26da83d62b11e9a25e5be7ce5e351230f6",
